.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MAC-HMAC 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_MAC-HMAC
.Nd The HMAC EVP_MAC implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing HMAC MACs through the
.Sy EVP_MAC
API.
.Pp
This implementation uses EVP_MD functions to get access to the
underlying digest.
.Ss Identity
This implementation is identified with this name and properties, to be
used with
.Xr EVP_MAC_fetch 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqHMAC", \(dqprovider=default" or \(dqprovider=fips"
.El
.Ss Supported parameters
The general description of these parameters can be found in
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 .
.Pp
The following parameters can be set with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
Sets the MAC key.
Setting this parameter is identical to passing a
.Em key
to
.Xr EVP_MAC_init 3 .
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Sets the name of the underlying digest to be used.
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Sets the properties to be queried when trying to fetch the underlying
digest.
This must be given together with the digest naming parameter ("digest",
or
.Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_DIGEST )
to be considered valid.
.It \(dqdigest-noinit" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_DIGEST_NOINIT Ns ) <integer>
A flag to set the MAC digest to not initialise the implementation
specific data.
The value 0 or 1 is expected.
This option is deprecated and will be removed in a future release.
It may be set but is currently ignored
.It \(dqdigest-oneshot" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_DIGEST_ONESHOT Ns ) <integer>
A flag to set the MAC digest to be a one-shot operation.
The value 0 or 1 is expected.
This option is deprecated and will be removed in a future release.
It may be set but is currently ignored.
.It \(dqtls-data-size" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_TLS_DATA_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqkey-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_FIPS_KEY_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
See
.Xr provider-mac 7 .
.El
.Pp
The following parameters can be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqsize" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
The "size" parameter can also be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_mac_size 3 .
The length of the "size" parameter is equal to that of an
.Sy unsigned int .
.It \(dqblock-size" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_BLOCK_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Gets the MAC block size.
The "block-size" parameter can also be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_block_size 3 .
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
See
.Xr provider-mac 7 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3 ,
.Xr HMAC 3
